                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0b9e6ee3-29b0-47b4-b1c4-7a3420b3490d",
                        "source_entry_id": "5c6af7fd-df28-3005-94e1-dd0afbade085",
                        "target_lang_word": "distinction",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "distinction",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f2ceb9bf-7ccb-34a0-8a90-d03a186a9019",
                                        "entry_id": "8d3bbf16-10b6-349a-8f11-63386baba581",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which distinguishes; a single occurrence of a determining factor or feature, the fact of being divided; separation, discrimination."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb380fdd-9c31-4956-ab00-34f4620e66f7",
                                                "sense_id": "f2ceb9bf-7ccb-34a0-8a90-d03a186a9019",
                                                "text": "The proper course for me, gentlemen of the jury, is to deal first with the earliest charges that have been falsely brought against me, and with my earliest accursers; and then with the later ones. I make this distinction because […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "44b940ec-0373-32df-80f4-07eaa9184007",
                                        "entry_id": "8d3bbf16-10b6-349a-8f11-63386baba581",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of distinguishing, discriminating; discrimination."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09c77ffd-c068-4e8c-a880-95cc2664f012",
                                                "sense_id": "44b940ec-0373-32df-80f4-07eaa9184007",
                                                "text": "There is a distinction to be made between resting and slacking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ab0e23e-b6c7-4ac3-8290-94f660897bf7",
                                                "sense_id": "44b940ec-0373-32df-80f4-07eaa9184007",
                                                "text": "In spite of these qualifications, the broad distinction between instinct and habit is undeniable. To take extreme cases, every animal at birth can take food by instinct, before it has had opportunity to learn; on the other hand, no one can ride a bicycle by instinct, though, after learning, the necessary movements become just as automatic as if they were instinctive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28c3772d-4949-4346-99b2-261ccddfecc8",
                                                "sense_id": "44b940ec-0373-32df-80f4-07eaa9184007",
                                                "text": "But, for practical purposes, it is possible to draw a distinction between a statement of facts observed and an expression of opinion as to the inference to be drawn from these facts, and the rule telling witnesses to state facts and not express opinions is of great value in keeping their statements out of the region of argument and conjecture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44399fec-5feb-4014-b638-febd3880392d",
                                                "sense_id": "44b940ec-0373-32df-80f4-07eaa9184007",
                                                "text": "This reflects a longtime distinction between \"good Jews\" and \"international Jews,\" drawn in a 1920 article by Winston Churchill, which put in the \"good category\" \"national Jews\" assimilated into British culture and Zionist Jews in Palestine, and into the malevolent one those who fueled \"this world-wide conspiracy for the overthrow of civilization.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3afa8c04-bbe9-441e-86d0-75f3a313c9d3",
                                                "sense_id": "44b940ec-0373-32df-80f4-07eaa9184007",
                                                "text": "Gedeon Van Rompay had the dubious distinction of being the only Site employee personally hired by Edwin Falkirk, former All Sections Chief and perennial piece of human trash. Lillian had found it easy not to hold this against the man, but only because there were so many other odious things about him to choose from. He was misogynist, he was chauvinistic, he was boorish, he was violent. Just about the only metric on which she rated Van Rompay higher than Falkirk was transphobia; the big man made no distinction between varieties of womanhood, feeling superior to all of them equally."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb6cd63c-98ae-3361-8d53-0714536a3da4",
                                        "entry_id": "8d3bbf16-10b6-349a-8f11-63386baba581",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A feature that causes someone or something to stand out from others of its type."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c79514eb-09ee-4bca-bf4b-1a60a1fc2350",
                                                "sense_id": "fb6cd63c-98ae-3361-8d53-0714536a3da4",
                                                "text": "Gedeon Van Rompay had the dubious distinction of being the only Site employee personally hired by Edwin Falkirk, former All Sections Chief and perennial piece of human trash. Lillian had found it easy not to hold this against the man, but only because there were so many other odious things about him to choose from. He was misogynist, he was chauvinistic, he was boorish, he was violent. Just about the only metric on which she rated Van Rompay higher than Falkirk was transphobia; the big man made no distinction between varieties of womanhood, feeling superior to all of them equally."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f589512-8351-3607-9d96-7c72be5d5945",
                                        "entry_id": "8d3bbf16-10b6-349a-8f11-63386baba581",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A feature that causes someone or something to stand out from others of its type.",
                                            "A feature that causes someone or something to stand out as being better; a mark of honour, rank, eminence or excellence; the quality of being distinguished."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "specifically",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60f579f6-dec5-441d-b01c-da6b6f279e7f",
                                                "sense_id": "0f589512-8351-3607-9d96-7c72be5d5945",
                                                "text": "She had the distinction of meeting the Queen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c18aa1f5-9090-4cbc-b3ff-1ebd3e6d31a2",
                                                "sense_id": "0f589512-8351-3607-9d96-7c72be5d5945",
                                                "text": "Mother[…]considered that the exclusiveness of Peter's circle was due not to its distinction, but to the fact that it was an inner Babylon of prodigality and whoredom, from which every Kensingtonian held aloof, except on the conventional tip-and-run excursions in pursuit of shopping, tea and theatres."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "daac009d-854d-4d00-bdc6-bdaf1dbd0ff6",
                                                "sense_id": "0f589512-8351-3607-9d96-7c72be5d5945",
                                                "text": "Leighton Baines, playing with distinction again, sent over a left-wing cross with pace and accuracy. Welbeck, prominently involved all night, could not reach it but Rooney was directly behind him, flashing his header past Szczesny."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a7c60e5f-9eae-4a68-b4c3-00739a1ce9ce",
                        "source_entry_id": "5c6af7fd-df28-3005-94e1-dd0afbade085",
                        "target_lang_word": "distinction",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "distinction",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "efdf1a8a-faca-3b36-b74d-db2b02996d98",
                                        "entry_id": "a602eb50-f9fd-3339-a8b2-395db2a1b978",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Action de séparer nettement une chose d’une autre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a155c0c-7e5e-489d-b55d-bb345f249818",
                                                "sense_id": "efdf1a8a-faca-3b36-b74d-db2b02996d98",
                                                "text": "Que le nombre important de naissances illégitimes soit une marque d'immoralité, je le veux bien ; encore est-il qu'il faut faire des distinctions et examiner si ce n'est pas plutôt un signe d'irrégularité que d'immoralité."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54d289c1-d855-4a7c-bb61-d547a6b3ab67",
                                                "sense_id": "efdf1a8a-faca-3b36-b74d-db2b02996d98",
                                                "text": "La distinction que l'on fait entre un astéroïde et une planète est purement arbitraire puisque fondée uniquement sur la dimension."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb192ff1-a60d-4193-ab41-ce16bd3834e6",
                                                "sense_id": "efdf1a8a-faca-3b36-b74d-db2b02996d98",
                                                "text": "Il faut donc distinguer entre deux situations, selon que l'enfant a la possession d’état d'enfant légitime ou non. Cette distinction est imposée par les articles 322 al. 2 et 334-9 du Code civil […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68c193bc-63ce-36dc-a475-42091c4333e8",
                                        "entry_id": "a602eb50-f9fd-3339-a8b2-395db2a1b978",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Indication, séparation des divers sens qu’une proposition peut recevoir."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bfcfba3-e74d-4192-a92f-a5b84f69487f",
                                                "sense_id": "68c193bc-63ce-36dc-a475-42091c4333e8",
                                                "text": "La casuistique dont Pascal s'est tant moqué n'était pas plus subtile et plus absurde que celle que l'on retrouve dans les polémiques entre ce qu'on nomme les écoles socialistes : Escobar aurait eu quelque peine à se reconnaître au milieu des distinctions de Jaurès ; […]. — (Georges Sorel, Réflexions sur la violence Chap.II, La décadence bourgeoise et la violence, 1908)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "600e8a98-4b7a-4546-84ec-f8126e9cab47",
                                                "sense_id": "68c193bc-63ce-36dc-a475-42091c4333e8",
                                                "text": "Mais ces distinctions hypothétiques sont dépourvues de fondement solide, et après avoir beaucoup varié sur la classification de l’hydrophobie, presque tout restait encore à faire pour la bien connaître."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a57d9910-cd0a-4b61-bfc4-8a7af3cf8e76",
                                                "sense_id": "68c193bc-63ce-36dc-a475-42091c4333e8",
                                                "text": "Il se tira d’affaire par une distinction subtile."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2fa05c43-c62c-3de0-a982-143b2da1c172",
                                        "entry_id": "a602eb50-f9fd-3339-a8b2-395db2a1b978",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Opération de l’esprit par laquelle on distingue une chose d'une autre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06c89567-a5ba-4fdb-90cc-a76ea0a32ba8",
                                                "sense_id": "2fa05c43-c62c-3de0-a982-143b2da1c172",
                                                "text": "La distinction des pensées ou connoissances, en médiates & immédiates prouve encore moins la prétendue imperceptibilité des pensées."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a542c4b-94dd-4ef0-ab54-2d3e30c6dc08",
                                                "sense_id": "2fa05c43-c62c-3de0-a982-143b2da1c172",
                                                "text": "En outre, la distinction opérable / inopérable se complique, certains cancers inopérables peuvent devenir accessibles à l’exérèse si celle-ci est couplée à la radiothérapie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da465256-4c3d-3541-81c0-41ed7a2a40cd",
                                        "entry_id": "a602eb50-f9fd-3339-a8b2-395db2a1b978",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Action de mettre une différence entre des personnes ou des choses, ou d’avoir égard à la différence qui est entre elles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2372a50-a5d4-4c9f-84de-25a6c37f28fa",
                                                "sense_id": "da465256-4c3d-3541-81c0-41ed7a2a40cd",
                                                "text": "Supprimé en 1870, rétabli par l'Assemblée nationale, le cautionnement est de nouveau supprimé pour tous les journaux sans distinction, par la loi de 1881."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea397b6d-5b83-49bd-b0fe-aca348d89d9a",
                                                "sense_id": "da465256-4c3d-3541-81c0-41ed7a2a40cd",
                                                "text": "Faire distinction de l’ami et de l’ennemi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36eaedb3-9c25-47d1-aab5-289c079e4e1f",
                                                "sense_id": "da465256-4c3d-3541-81c0-41ed7a2a40cd",
                                                "text": "Je fais grande distinction entre l’un et l’autre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c025060b-5228-3937-96f1-ee7a479bfa8c",
                                        "entry_id": "a602eb50-f9fd-3339-a8b2-395db2a1b978",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ce qui établit ou indique une différence entre des personnes ou des choses."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "07f3a105-f816-4b4d-a563-8c6c0ac9c7c0",
                                                "sense_id": "c025060b-5228-3937-96f1-ee7a479bfa8c",
                                                "text": "La distinction des rangs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcc65f2e-9baf-48f8-9fdc-a170acc66e62",
                                                "sense_id": "c025060b-5228-3937-96f1-ee7a479bfa8c",
                                                "text": "Les distinctions sociales."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb6f06e6-2662-4f06-974b-b55b1c17dab9",
                                                "sense_id": "c025060b-5228-3937-96f1-ee7a479bfa8c",
                                                "text": "Toutes ces distinctions disparurent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ddc2358a-7037-351d-961e-365a521bbcff",
                                        "entry_id": "a602eb50-f9fd-3339-a8b2-395db2a1b978",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Prérogative, honneur ou marque de préférence, d’estime ou d’égard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03b92498-341f-4cdc-b101-8fe25c8270d6",
                                                "sense_id": "ddc2358a-7037-351d-961e-365a521bbcff",
                                                "text": "Il aime les distinctions très flatteuses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b569273-e8be-44d8-8d9a-c8f575914f63",
                                                "sense_id": "ddc2358a-7037-351d-961e-365a521bbcff",
                                                "text": "Traiter quelqu’un avec distinction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae0ac4e5-3551-36bc-9792-32107cb0695a",
                                        "entry_id": "a602eb50-f9fd-3339-a8b2-395db2a1b978",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Bon ton, élégance ou dignité des manières."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f0a9fc7-32d5-4471-b7e2-2c8d3ffad075",
                                                "sense_id": "ae0ac4e5-3551-36bc-9792-32107cb0695a",
                                                "text": "Un air de distinction."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0acdb300-397b-4a55-95a8-1f8abbe1a0b0",
                                                "sense_id": "ae0ac4e5-3551-36bc-9792-32107cb0695a",
                                                "text": "Il a beaucoup de distinction."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ecd16e8-296f-4f34-adda-dc84202da065",
                                                "sense_id": "ae0ac4e5-3551-36bc-9792-32107cb0695a",
                                                "text": "Il manque de distinction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
